/Kaggle/kagglehub/blob/main/README.md\n\nimport kagglehub\n# kagglehub.dataset_download('<owner>/<dataset-slug>')","metadata":{"_uuid":"8f2839f25d086af736a60e9eeb907d3b93b6e0e5","_cell_guid":"b1076dfc-b9ad-4769-8c92-a6c4dae69d19","trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-10T14:18:27.941173Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-10T14:18:27.941379Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-10T14:18:29.998456Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-10T14:18:27.941347Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-10T14:18:29.99784Z"},"jupyter":{"source_hidden":true}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Cyclistic Bike-Share Case Study: Converting Casual Riders to Annual Members\n\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Introduction\n**Purpose and Scenario:**\nThis case study is conducted for **Cyclistic**, a fictional bike-share company based in Chicago featuring over 5,800 bicycles and 600 docking stations. As a junior data analyst working on the marketing analyst team under Director Lily Moreno, the core business objective is driven by a critical realization: the company's future economic growth and success depend heavily on maximizing the number of annual memberships, as annual members are significantly more profitable than casual riders. \n\n**The Real-World Obstacle & Strategy:**\nRather than launching a broad marketing campaign to target entirely new customers, the marketing team identified a prime opportunity to convert existing casual riders—who are already familiar with the program and use the bikes for their mobility needs—into dedicated annual members. However, before executive leadership can approve any strategic marketing programs, the recommendations must be rigorously backed by compelling data insights and professional visualizations. \n\n**Analytical Framework:**\nTo tackle this business challenge, this project strictly follows the industry-standard six-step data analysis process outlined in the Google Data Analytics framework: **Ask, Prepare, Process, Analyze, Share, and Act**.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Problems\n**Major Problem Identification:**\nThe primary problem under investigation is defined by the first guiding question assigned by management: **\"How do annual members and casual riders use Cyclistic bikes differently?\"** Without isolating these behavioral patterns, the team cannot design targeted digital media strategies.\n\n**Analysis Approach & Data Scope:**\nTo uncover these behavioral gaps, I am utilizing *Python (Pandas)* to process and analyze historical trip data covering the past 12 consecutive months, spanning from September 2025 through August 2026.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import pandas as pd\n\n# List of all 12 monthly CSV files with the exact dataset path\nfiles = [\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202501-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202509-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202510-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202511-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202512-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202602-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202603-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202604-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202605-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202606-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202607-divvy-tripdata.csv',\n    '/kaggle/input/datasets/imran495/cyclistic-bike-trips-2025-2026/202608-divvy-tripdata.csv'\n]\n\n# Read all monthly CSV files into a list of DataFrames\ndf_list = [pd.read_csv(file) for file in files]\n\n# Concatenate all dataframes into a single master DataFrame\nbike_trips_df = pd.concat(df_list, ignore_index=True)\n\n# Verify the successful import by printing total rows and columns\nprint(\"Total rows and columns:\", bike_trips_df.shape)\nbike_trips_df.head()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-10T19:24:25.803194Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-10T19:24:25.803609Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-10T19:24:52.979928Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-10T19:24:25.80358Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-10T19:24:52.979036Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Data Naming Convention Note:** \nPlease note that due to a naming convention inconsistency in the raw repository source, the file corresponding to January 2026 is named `202501-divvy-tripdata.csv`. However, internal data verification confirms that the records correctly belong to January 2026. This has been fully accounted for to preserve the strict continuity of the 12-month timeline (September 2025 through August 2026).","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Data Integrity and Cleaning Process (Process Phase Logging):**\nTo ensure the data is reliable, credible, and free of errors, the following technical pipeline is executed within the notebook cells below:\n* **Data Integration & Uniformity:** Importing multiple CSV data files and standardizing column structures to combine them into a unified Pandas DataFrame.\n* **Handling Missing Values & Blanks:** Scanning for null entries, empty strings, and structural anomalies to prevent calculation distortion.\n* **Removing Duplicates:** Filtering out duplicate trip entries to maintain high data integrity.\n* **Data Transformation:** Engineering new analytical columns—specifically `ride_length` (calculating trip duration by subtracting start time from end time) and `day_of_week` (identifying the specific day each ride initiated)—to enable deep exploratory analysis.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Step 1: Convert started_at and ended_at columns to datetime objects\nbike_trips_df['started_at'] = pd.to_datetime(bike_trips_df['started_at'])\nbike_trips_df['ended_at'] = pd.to_datetime(bike_trips_df['ended_at'])\n\n# Step 2: Create 'ride_length' column (trip duration in seconds, then converted to minutes for readability)\nbike_trips_df['ride_length'] = (bike_trips_df['ended_at'] - bike_trips_df['started_at']).dt.total_seconds() / 60\n\n# Step 3: Create 'day_of_week' column (1 = Sunday, 7 = Saturday)\nbike_trips_df['day_of_week'] = bike_trips_df['started_at'].dt.dayofweek + 1\n\n# Step 4: Drop any bad data where ride_length is negative or zero (e.g., dock maintenance tests)\nbike_trips_df = bike_trips_df[bike_trips_df['ride_length'] > 0]\n\n# Step 5: Verify the cleaned data shape and new columns\nprint(\"Data shape after cleaning and adding columns:\", bike_trips_df.shape)\nbike_trips_df[['ride_id', 'started_at', 'ended_at', 'ride_length', 'day_of_week', 'member_casual']].head()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-10T19:27:31.761411Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-10T19:27:31.762211Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-10T19:27:36.593015Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-10T19:27:31.762179Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-10T19:27:36.592302Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Solutions\n*Proposed Solution:* To convert casual riders into annual members, Cyclistic should launch targeted digital media campaigns focused on the behavioral differences uncovered in our 12-month analysis. Specifically, since casual riders take significantly longer trips (averaging ~20.7 minutes compared to ~12.4 minutes for members) and peak heavily during weekends, marketing initiatives should introduce weekend-focused promotional bundles, leisure-to-commuter loyalty incentives, and digital app notifications highlighting cost savings for longer recreational rides.\n*Alternatives:* We also evaluated broad-spectrum billboard and transit station advertisements targeting general tourists; however, this approach lacks personalized engagement and yields lower conversion efficiency compared to digital media.\n*Pros and Cons:* Digital app-based promotions offer high precision, direct tracking, and cost-effectiveness, though they require active user engagement on the mobile app. Broad advertisements build general brand awareness but fail to capture direct conversion metrics.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Step 1: Summary statistics of 'ride_length' for all riders\nprint(\"--- Overall Ride Length Summary (Minutes) ---\")\nprint(bike_trips_df['ride_length'].describe())\n\n# Step 2: Compare average ride length between members and casual riders\nprint(\"\\n--- Average Ride Length by Rider Type ---\")\navg_ride_length = bike_trips_df.groupby('member_casual')['ride_length'].mean()\nprint(avg_ride_length)\n\n# Step 3: Compare max ride length between members and casual riders\nprint(\"\\n--- Maximum Ride Length by Rider Type ---\")\nmax_ride_length = bike_trips_df.groupby('member_casual')['ride_length'].max()\nprint(max_ride_length)\n\n# Step 4: Find the mode (most frequent) day of the week for each rider type\nprint(\"\\n--- Most Frequent Day of Week by Rider Type (1=Sun, 7=Sat) ---\")\nmode_day = bike_trips_df.groupby('member_casual')['day_of_week'].agg(lambda x: x.mode().iloc[0])\nprint(mode_day)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-10T19:30:18.91939Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-10T19:30:18.920383Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-10T19:30:20.567671Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-10T19:30:18.920343Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-10T19:30:20.566022Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Step 1: Import visualization libraries\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\n\n# Set visual style\nsns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n\n# Step 2: Plot 1 - Average Ride Length Comparison (Members vs Casual)\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\navg_ride_plot = bike_trips_df.groupby('member_casual')['ride_length'].mean().plot(kind='bar', color=['skyblue', 'salmon'])\nplt.title('Average Ride Length: Casual Riders vs. Annual Members', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\nplt.xlabel('Rider Type', fontsize=12)\nplt.ylabel('Average Ride Length (Minutes)', fontsize=12)\nplt.xticks(rotation=0)\nplt.show()\n\n# Step 3: Plot 2 - Number of Rides by Day of the Week for Each Rider Type\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\nsns.countplot(data=bike_trips_df, x='day_of_week', hue='member_casual', palette='Set2')\nplt.title('Total Rides by Day of the Week', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\nplt.xlabel('Day of Week (1 = Sunday, 7 = Saturday)', fontsize=12)\nplt.ylabel('Total Number of Rides', fontsize=12)\nplt.legend(title='Rider Type')\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-10T19:35:17.972562Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-10T19:35:17.972904Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-10T19:35:37.626724Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-10T19:35:17.972876Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-10T19:35:37.625757Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"> As visualized, casual riders take longer weekend trips, whereas annual members exhibit stable weekday commuting trends.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Conclusion\n*Key Takeaways:* The 12-month historical data analysis reveals distinct usage patterns: annual members primarily utilize bikes for weekday commuting (peaking mid-week), whereas casual riders predominantly use bikes for longer leisure and recreational trips during weekends. Addressing these distinct behavioral gaps provides a clear roadmap for targeted marketing interventions.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Next Steps\n*Recommendations:* \n1. Launch targeted weekend digital promotions within the Cyclistic app targeting frequent casual riders.\n2. Introduce a transitional \"Leisure-to-Member\" pass that credits weekend ride fees toward an annual membership.\n3. Partner with local Chicago recreational hubs for digital QR-code marketing campaigns.\n*Action Plan:* The marketing analytics team will collaborate with Lily Moreno to design the campaign wireframes over the next two weeks, with the pilot digital rollout scheduled for the upcoming quarter to measure conversion rates.","metadata":{}}]}